  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:single-turn-inference",
  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "The stateless request-response mode of using a language model: a prompt goes in, one completion comes out, and the interaction ends \u2014 with no intermediate tool execution, environmental feedback, self-correction, or persistent state; it is the cheapest and most predictable inference pattern, suited to classification, extraction, translation, and summarisation, and serves as the baseline against which iterative agentic workflows are defined and evaluated.",
